<p>And yet again: the way the article is written now makes it sound like the ritual is NOT necessarily the same each time. So there's a lengthy list of requirements. Does each book lovingly describe each ritual in detail, listing exactly what the requirements are and stating specifically that &quot;s/he carefully sliced a quarter-moon shape into the left buttock while spitting into the open wound&quot; or somesuch? Because that <em>would</em> make it easier to identify, <em>but the article as written doesn't state that</em>.</p>
