<p>&quot;Twenty-four (24) seconds after the birth of the intended Foundation Hero, codenamed 'Hero George', all copies of the book underwent a spontaneous combustion event. In their place were left a boxed set of adventure novels detailing how 'Agent George' rose to an illustrious career with the Foundation and became O5-[REDACTED] following [REDACTED], whereupon he took pity upon the 'Tattered Monster' in the tank of hydrochloric acid and released it, a decision directly leading to [REDACTED], [REDACTED] and his ritualised murder by his fellow O5s in revenge. Attempts to recall all copies, cover up the resulting security breach and prevent the realisation of the described events are ongoing.&quot;</p>
<p>While this would be awesome, it would lock 682's existence into a certainty for the next fifty years or so unless they found a way to undo the effect, so I don't think it would match the canon idea that the Foundation don't <em>know</em> that their next attempt won't destroy the rascal.</p>

